      <activity id="0e5367a5-6f8e-5532-93ef-54243b5e38c0" activityNameId="22d19579-2d77-5c1c-8996-92f502766113" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, overflow element, steel, approx. 40 m3/h</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, overflow element, steel, approx. 40 m3/h
Disposal of an overflow element made of galvanised steel insulated with rubber. Installation e.g. above door separating the rooms- Weight per element 1.1 kg;
UUID: 7cf7b6f3-3d1c-47e3-b55d-706a54502ae2
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces and copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Questionnaire and assumptions. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7cf7b6f3-3d1c-47e3-b55d-706a54502ae2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
